  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-08-05T21:17:12.723Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "1. Open VRChat\n\n2. Use the hand tracking, either through VD or something else\n\n3. Open the quick menu. Notice it always opens at the same angle. Wish this was either bound to your hand or based on the angle you're using it at like the main menu.\n\n4. Go and turn on Horizon adjust. Lie down.\n\n5. Pinch-movement gestures do not work unless you are upright in real life, no matter your horizon adjust settings.\n\nThe Hand Tracking gestures are pretty much unresponsive unless you are sitting up. So I can't lie back and watch a movie or something with Horizon Adjust. Also using the Quick Menu is really hard since it floats in the same spot, even when the main menu is set to follow your head movement.",
